  "slug": "archaea-duplication-d927",
  "summary": "Cross-species alignments and orthology now recover coding sequences and protein family content beyond per-genome reference annotation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is defining coding content from cross-genome evidence rather than relying solely on per-genome reference annotation. Genomes2Genes converts Progressive Cactus whole-genome alignments into validated coding sequence alignments for extant and ancestral species. The gbe study maps verified protein complex components to orthogroups across 31 eukaryotes, identifying 184 universal orthogroups and conserved and taxon-restricted orthogroup expansions, and releases the PCOC suite for detecting them. PANTHER 2027 extends protein family phylogenetic trees and GO annotations across 131 genomes, with a 20%-100% coverage gain in annotations. What is new is the joint use of genomic alignment, orthology, and family-level evidence to delimit coding content independently of a single reference annotation. The works differ in organism, data type, and objective, so this reflects a shared strategy rather than a common method.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-14"
}
